Estimates are focused person-hours, not guarantees. AI reduces typing time but not account setup, access failures, understanding schemas, or validating outputs. The full sequence below is **31–57 hours after pre-work**, so a solo 24-hour event requires substantial cuts; even a 36–48-hour event needs strict scope control and rest. Check event rules before doing project-specific pre-work.

| Phase | Work and concrete completion criterion | Estimate | Dependencies / interchangeability |
|---|---|---|---|
| **0. Allowed pre-work and setup** | Verify hackathon rules; create cloud project, billing alerts, GCS bucket, BigQuery datasets, credentials, and model access. Install Python, Git, Docker/WSL as applicable, dbt adapter, and Airflow environment. Choose local host or an approved VM, not both. Obtain consented/redacted sample screenshots and candidate benchmark files if permitted. Confirm Docker and a warehouse query work. | **4–8 h**, outside event only if allowed | Account setup, tool tutorials, and dataset scouting can be independent. A VM is optional; local Airflow plus hosted/demo Streamlit is sufficient. |
